+## Explicit uncapped Codex operation (WP-02 / WP-03, 2026-09-19)
+
+This is a separate policy from `ModelCallBudget`. It implements the recorded D3
+choice of **no business monetary/global-call ceiling**, without fabricated prices,
+infinite numeric allowances or `cost_bound_attested`. The original priced path
+is unchanged. No real provider, credential or user-database operation is enabled
+merely by installing this source. Only BTC/ETH requests explicitly labeled with
+protocol `codex-cli-0.155.1-pal-v1` can use the new path; do not relabel/recreate an
+already claimed request. Unknown invoices and provider request counts stay null.
+
+### Explicit local profile, never credential discovery
+
+`research_codex_local.CodexLocalProfile` requires an absolute executable path,
+its operator-reviewed SHA256, an explicit dedicated `codex_home`, a separate
+private `workspace_parent`, an exact model ID and a 1..600 second I/O timeout.
+Only the official native **Codex CLI 0.155.1** protocol is supported; both binary
+hash and `--version` are checked on each invocation. No PATH search, installation,
+model discovery or automatic upgrade is performed. Model reasoning effort is
+explicitly `max` and fast mode is disabled; unsupported model/settings fail, not
+fall back. Supporting another CLI or version needs a separately tested adapter.
+
+The six-field nonsecret UTF-8 JSON profile is read only from the explicitly
+supplied `--codex-profile` file (at most 16 KiB). Paths are configuration, not
+business persistence. Its shape is:
+
+```json
+{
+  "executable": "C:\\ApprovedTools\\codex.exe",
+  "executable_sha256": "<operator-verified binary SHA256>",
+  "codex_home": "C:\\PrivateResearch\\CodexAuth",
+  "workspace_parent": "C:\\PrivateResearch\\CodexScratch",
+  "model_id": "<explicit approved model ID>",
+  "timeout_seconds": 180
+}
+```
+
+Placeholders are not executable configuration. Do not put keys in this file,
+arguments, repository or chat. The operator must establish the dedicated private
+auth directory through an authorized local login procedure; this wrapper neither
+reads/copies credentials nor imports another coding session. The CLI itself may
+use/update its selected authentication state, installation metadata and temporary
+auth housekeeping. It is not accurate to promise that this directory is untouched.
+
+Native tools, shell, apps, plugins, hooks, MCP and host-skill discovery are disabled
+in a restrictive local model catalog/config. Each invocation receives a new
+private working directory with an empty Git boundary, a fresh ephemeral session,
+allowlisted environment, and the **exact original messages_json** plus fixed
+research action definitions. Original evidence is not truncated or rewritten to
+fit a provider. Native tools are not used to research; the existing application
+executes only its approved snapshot actions returned as strict structured JSON.
+
+`--ignore-user-config` does not disable global auth-directory instructions in this
+pinned version. The adapter therefore rejects `AGENTS.md`, `AGENTS.override.md`
+and `managed_config.toml` in the selected auth home. It also rejects system
+`config.toml`, `requirements.toml` and `managed_config.toml` in `/etc/codex` on
+Linux or the OS-known `ProgramData/OpenAI/Codex` directory on Windows. Presence
+or unreadability blocks; files are not opened, deleted, disabled or rewritten.
+An empty MCP-table override is **not** proof that inherited servers disappeared.
+Managed installations need separate reviewed support, not policy bypass flags.
+macOS/other platform profiles are not supported by this implementation.
+
+The pinned CLI's own transient state databases/logs are directed to the private
+scratch directory and removed after a normal/handled invocation. These are CLI
+infrastructure, **not an alternate durable store for project business evidence**.
+The project's authorization, claims, outcomes and research remain in the same
+native PostgreSQL. Hard process termination can leave private scratch remnants;
+there is no automatic cross-process scavenger or secure-erasure claim. Auth and
+scratch directories, native binaries and raw client logs must never be uploaded.
+
+### Immutable authorization and shared replay protection
+
+`UncappedModelAuthorization` binds the exact profile digest, model, expiry,
+1..100 explicit `(record_id, request_sha256)` entries and a message-byte ceiling.
+`uncapped_cost_approved=True` is required; the output mode is explicitly
+`observed_after_response`. The bounded roster is an admission/codec boundary,
+not a business quota. Existing per-task calls, context, tokens, deadline and
+worker/stop controls remain; new authorizations are never generated automatically.
+
+```python
+from polymarket_alpha_lab.research_uncapped_authorization import UncappedModelAuthorization
+
+# All names below are explicitly reviewed application inputs, not inferred defaults.
+policy = UncappedModelAuthorization(
+    authorization_id=approved_authorization_id,
+    model_id=profile.model_id,
+    profile_sha256=profile.content_sha256,
+    expires_at=approved_expiry,
+    request_keys=tuple((r.record_id, r.content_sha256) for r in reviewed_requests),
+    uncapped_cost_approved=True,
+)
+with ProjectPostgres(actual_project_root).session() as research:
+    research.create_uncapped_authorization(policy=policy, allow_authorization_write=True)
+    result = research.run_uncapped_research(
+        request=reviewed_requests[0], authorization_id=policy.authorization_id,
+        profile=profile, allow_model_calls=True,
+    )
+    usage = research.inspect_uncapped_authorization(authorization_id=policy.authorization_id)
+```
+
+The existing execution claim commits first. A new append-only invocation permit
+then commits before entering the CLI; its `(record_id, call_number)` is the SAME
+unique key used by capped budgets. New uncapped columns require null budget ID,
+null monetary charge and null priced sequence, never zero-price substitution.
+Changing policy or switching modes cannot reuse a lost original ordinal. The
+trigger also refuses mixed modes for later ordinals of the same claimed request.
+
+Validated CLI usage is committed before the next action is returned to the agent.
+Input/output usage is retained; cached/cache-write/reasoning values are subsets,
+not added twice. A failed invocation has unknown usage, not zero. A reservation
+with no outcome stays unknown after process loss or uncertain acknowledgement;
+no refund, resend, reassignment or guessed recovery occurs. Completed, failed and
+incomplete research still replay the original record without entering a client.
+Policy and profile are copied/revalidated; no transaction is held across model I/O.
+
+This extends the existing catalog with **migration 68**,
+`20260919000000_research_uncapped_codex.sql`. Original67 SQL payloads and all old
+records are preserved; existing permissions/transaction guards apply to the new
+append-only tables. The isolated native proof upgrades67->68 and checks old capped
+history, two-team real-CLI/mock-server turns, stopped/replayed turns, failure,
+crash-after-permit and cross-mode rejection. It does not migrate a user's database.
+Do not overwrite an old kit or copy `.local`; existing version-switch restrictions
+still apply and an authorized concrete upgrade must be handled separately.
+
+### What the adapter proves, and what it does not
+
+One application `complete` launches one `exec`, with no outer retry, repair,
+resume, new task ID or fallback. The custom `pal_codex` provider uses the pinned
+CLI's OpenAI authentication and default endpoint selection; it does not override
+a reserved built-in provider or choose an arbitrary production URL. HTTP/SSE
+retry settings are explicitly zero and native tools are absent in tested requests.
+Real pinned-binary synthetic cases exercise success,429,500,broken stream and
+invalid JSON; their observed request counts do not certify every possible
+internal CLI/auth/provider behavior. **A CLI invocation is not a certified count
+of billable provider submissions.** Provider counts and actual fees remain null.
+
+The CLI protocol does not provide an attested provider-enforced output-token
+ceiling for this adapter. The ceiling is requested in the task and checked AFTER
+receipt; overruns/malformed outputs fail without a second request. Do not use this
+adapter under a priced single-operation hard-bound attestation. Unknown or failed
+usage is omitted from validated totals and exposed as failed/unknown counts;
+`reported_total_tokens` is not a complete provider invoice or economic limit.
+
+Stdout (1 MiB), stderr (64 KiB), event count, schema and I/O time are bounded.
+Only one complete terminal turn with allowed research actions and valid usage is
+accepted; native tool activity, duplicate/partial results and unexpected events
+are rejected. Native reasoning and raw stderr are discarded, not logged into
+research evidence. Linux owns a new process group; Windows assigns a kill-on-close
+Job Object before sending the prompt. The owning child/descendants are cleaned up
+on handled failures, including descendant-held pipes. OS creation/filesystem
+latency, repeated hard interrupts, malicious same-user races, administrators and
+arbitrary hostile binaries are not a universal sandbox or real-time guarantee.
+The executable starts before Windows job assignment; this is not prevention of
+all pre-assignment activity by a hostile executable. Preserve OS security rules.
+
